{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjxQfq9hQ6faUp9vhoPW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything on the checklist is now verified on the final build. No source edits were made after this build; the HTML was last rebuilt at this point.\n\n**Test results on the final build**\n- **Node suite:** 610 checks, 0 failed, including the scripted full playthrough (New Game through all 11 cases, the ending and the credits).\n- **Hub harness:** all four runs pass, plus the standalone check.\n- **Browser:** Chromium 15 checks, Firefox and WebKit 12-second plays (3 checks), and the Pixel 7 and iPhone 13 phone profiles (10 checks), all passing.\n\n**Defects found and fixed this pass**\n- **Cinematics:** the leftover painted dots and the stray cane line in the gala and final-table cinematics are gone. The gala frame is confirmed clean.\n- **Tutorial panel:** it covered the monitor and, during Code Blue, the shock timing. It now sits lower and hides during Code Blue, the closing dressing, and dev mode.\n- **Lightbox note:** the sticky note was cut off (\"Hernia. Ob\") and now wraps.\n- **Dev panel:** its slider values sat a row off and are now aligned. They are still tight against the labels for \"Slip damage\" and \"Syringe dose\".\n\n**Screenshot coverage at 1920×1080**\n- I looked at: title, menu, difficulty, story, chart, lightbox, the operation HUD, the tool wheel, Code Blue, dev mode, Case Files, lobby, About, Results, Lost, both wards, and four of the five cinematics.\n- I did not look at the credits screen, the Hub card, the Settings screen, or the 2560×1440 and 3440×1440 frames. Those ran with no errors and passed the size checks, but I never viewed them.\n- The ER ending cinematic was looked at before the last two cinematic edits.\n\n**Stubs and fidelity gaps**\n- The code contains no stubs or TODO text; the content check greps the source for TODO, FIXME, placeholder and stub.\n- Some art is simpler than the plan describes: the cinematics are short rigged scenes with a few painted props, and the ship's ward is a compact map reusing Ward 3's props.\n\nThe three deliverables are in the work folder: the single HTML file, `exit-interview.json`, and the dev folder. The Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback are in my earlier reply and in the About screen."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":354,"cache_read_input_tokens":573362,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":354},"output_tokens":750,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73cf9888-9422-42e0-82aa-d7becfd7d585","uuid":"20c5745c-dcf1-4cf2-b0c4-97b1cd2df643","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:41:32.594Z","request_id":"req_011CgjxQfSbNdBTnQ6w7LsNN"}
