{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjymUmqcfJGGwUdMtsdK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The earlier crashes were memory pressure from other agents' processes on the shared machine. The cinematic code is the same set of cinematics I checked before. Verification of that build is mostly from earlier runs. Once memory freed up, I re-ran the four cinematic scenes in one session (0 errors), the Chromium checks (15) and the 2-player Hub run (32).\n\n**This pass**\n- I tried adding more rigged characters to the cinematics: a rigged patient and nurses on the gurney, Dr. Hale and guests at the gala, a deckhand and nurse on the ship, and a sixth doctor at the final table.\n- Headless Chromium then crashed while loading them. I couldn't tell whether the extra rigs or the memory pressure caused it, because the crash continued after I took the extra rigs back out.\n- I rolled them back, so the five cinematics are exactly as before. They are still short scenes with a few rigged characters over painted stages and a few painted props.\n\n**Verified**\n- **Memory:** the shared machine had 18 GB of 20 GB in use. The crashes stopped once it dropped.\n- **Cinematic scenes:** all four (gurney, gala, storm, final table) run with 0 errors in one session. This is the first time since the extra-rig edits that I confirmed they load.\n- **Node fast suite:** 605 checks, 0 failed (this run was during the crashes).\n- **Chromium:** 15 checks, 0 failed.\n- **2-player Hub run:** 32 checks, 0 failed.\n\n**Not re-run on this exact build**\n- The full playthrough.\n- The 4-player and server Hub runs.\n- The Firefox, WebKit and phone checks.\n\nTheir last passing runs were on the build before the rolled-back edits, whose code is identical.\n\n**Still short of PLAN.md**\n- Richer rig-driven cinematics are not built.\n- Credits, Settings, the Hub card, the ER ending and the 3440×1440 frame were each checked in a single screenshot.\n\nThe deliverables are in the work folder: the single HTML file, `exit-interview.json`, and the dev folder."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":438,"cache_read_input_tokens":623722,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":438},"output_tokens":699,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73cf9888-9422-42e0-82aa-d7becfd7d585","uuid":"447336f3-6687-429e-b7a0-4f5035ebfaa5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:59:21.109Z","request_id":"req_011CgjymUNHGS2hhPU26DYTa"}
